<%#
    Skip link — WCAG 2.4.1 Bypass Blocks.

    Included as the FIRST child of <body> on every page, ahead of
    nav-dashboard, so it is the first focusable element in the document.
    It used to live in main-header.ejs, which every template includes
    *after* the sidebar; that made it the 10th tab stop, behind the whole
    sidebar including Logout, so the bypass mechanism sat behind the block
    it was meant to bypass.

    The target is the page's own main landmark. Every page template gives
    its <main> id="main" tabindex="-1" so the fragment resolves and focus
    actually moves.
-%>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>
